<title>UK: Silver fixes at fresh low since November 1993.</title>
<headline>Silver fixes at fresh low since November 1993.</headline>
<text>
<p>SILVER - Fixed at 422.35 cents vs 431.75 cents previously. Fresh low since November 3, 1993. Sold by funds last night. Market short. May test 400 cents.</p>
<p>GOLD - Recovered slightly from lower opening. In $318-$322 range with downside favoured medium term.</p>
<p>PLATINUM - Steady after light selling. $403.00/$407.00.</p>
<p>PALLADIUM - Touch easier at $173.00/$177.00 down $3.75.</p>
</text>
